WEBVTT

00:03.770 --> 00:06.970
You wanted to show us what a 
boss fight looks like, first?

00:07.280 --> 00:10.340
That's part of it. But not all.

00:12.130 --> 00:13.820
My leg!

00:17.230 --> 00:19.310
Even if you lose, you won't die.

00:20.290 --> 00:22.400
Like I said.

00:22.400 --> 00:26.000
There's no shame for an adventurer 
in avoiding a fight you can't win.

00:27.410 --> 00:29.220
Maybe you're right.

00:29.220 --> 00:32.170
But no, that's not what I meant!

00:32.610 --> 00:37.130
If I run away here, I don't 
think I'll ever come back.

00:38.160 --> 00:40.960
I'll never be a real adventurer.

00:41.670 --> 00:42.900
Ryze...

00:43.700 --> 00:45.770
You've made your decision, then.

02:21.530 --> 02:25.790
<b> Magical
Contract</b>

02:44.830 --> 02:46.220
A Grand Slime...

02:49.400 --> 02:51.710
We won't mess up like those guys did.

02:51.710 --> 02:54.890
Let's be the ones to tell 
the guild we beat it!

02:55.470 --> 02:57.370
<i>This didn't go like I was hoping.</i>

02:57.370 --> 03:00.960
<i>There's no actual need to 
beat the boss for this exam.</i>

03:02.130 --> 03:07.100
<i>Honestly, I was hoping those other 
examinees would beat it for us.</i>

03:07.690 --> 03:12.410
<i>But, well, it's important to 
encounter some challenges in life.</i>

03:16.580 --> 03:18.680
I can see through your attacks!

03:18.680 --> 03:20.050
Aim for its core!

03:30.640 --> 03:32.950
Focus on empowering your magic.

03:34.140 --> 03:39.290
<i>These two are capable of 
defeating a Grand Slime.</i>

03:40.220 --> 03:44.070
Listen to me. Physical attacks 
will barely work at all.

03:44.070 --> 03:47.300
Magic's what you'll need to win.

03:47.760 --> 03:50.370
Can you use powerful fire magic?

03:50.370 --> 03:52.390
Yes, a little...

03:52.390 --> 03:55.790
But it'll take time to activate.

03:55.790 --> 03:57.290
Don't worry.

03:57.290 --> 03:59.870
I'll block its attacks while you're casting.

03:59.870 --> 04:03.790
Wait. Can you let me be the one to do that?

04:08.430 --> 04:12.810
Rentt, help Ryze! I'm fine on my own!

04:25.700 --> 04:26.400
Here I go!

04:29.540 --> 04:31.280
Grand Pyrox!

04:49.560 --> 04:50.950
We got it!

04:50.950 --> 04:52.740
Finish it before it regenerates!

04:52.740 --> 04:53.680
Right!

05:00.140 --> 05:02.820
We did it!

05:02.820 --> 05:05.280
Yeah. We beat the boss!

05:07.730 --> 05:09.130
Rentt?

05:09.130 --> 05:12.750
Slime fluids are worth a lot.

05:12.750 --> 05:13.570
Let's gather them up.

05:14.840 --> 05:18.640
Even if we split the money among the three 
of us, we'll get at least one silver each.

05:24.520 --> 05:25.630
See you there!

05:26.290 --> 05:27.860
Well, I don't think it matters.

05:28.790 --> 05:31.510
I knew you'd figure it out.

05:37.240 --> 05:38.810
Just like I thought.

05:38.810 --> 05:41.280
A sleeping gas trap?

05:41.280 --> 05:44.940
Right before the goal is one of the 
places people let their guard down most.

05:45.310 --> 05:49.310
Not that it really matters if 
they get there ahead of us.

05:49.990 --> 05:51.530
What do you mean?

05:51.530 --> 05:56.970
Getting there first doesn't 
mean passing, does it?

05:57.560 --> 05:59.400
Think back really carefully.

05:59.400 --> 06:02.530
The guild didn't say a word about that.

06:03.050 --> 06:07.130
Your job is to reach the 
point written on your map.

06:07.410 --> 06:13.100
The first party to arrive will receive 
a reward befitting their efforts.

06:14.030 --> 06:19.840
They set it up so we'd think 
it was a race, but...

06:19.840 --> 06:23.380
That's why Rentt didn't mind 
letting the other party go ahead,

06:23.380 --> 06:25.980
even when we were in front of the boss room.

06:25.980 --> 06:27.960
That's a mean trap.

06:27.960 --> 06:29.660
I feel stupid for worrying.

06:30.050 --> 06:36.150
An adventurer's only job is to complete 
the task before the deadline.

06:36.150 --> 06:40.010
It wouldn't have killed 
them to tell us that.

06:40.340 --> 06:45.570
You can't be a real adventurer 
unless you can think for yourself.

06:49.040 --> 06:50.690
Congratulations.

06:50.690 --> 06:52.800
You're the first here.

06:53.290 --> 06:54.660
Are you real?

06:54.660 --> 06:57.390
Show us proof you're with the guild.

06:58.920 --> 07:00.820
Is this enough for you?

07:00.820 --> 07:03.260
Yes. Thank you.

07:04.620 --> 07:07.060
Take these, then.

07:07.530 --> 07:13.510
Show these to the guild's front desk and 
you'll become Bronze-class adventurers.

07:16.300 --> 07:19.950
Hey, what's that bonus that 
you guys talked about?

07:19.950 --> 07:24.330
Oh, the first three teams 
get a little bonus.

07:24.330 --> 07:27.540
Here. Potions and a case for them.

07:28.490 --> 07:30.450
I've been wanting one of these!

07:31.720 --> 07:34.050
So that's what that was about.

07:34.050 --> 07:35.650
Hey, you two.

07:36.900 --> 07:41.190
Can we make a side trip before we go home?

07:45.490 --> 07:48.320
This is the 2nd floor, right?

07:48.800 --> 07:50.820
Do you know what it's like?

07:50.820 --> 07:51.730
No.

07:52.540 --> 07:56.440
The labyrinths are beyond 
human understanding.

07:56.440 --> 07:58.750
You'll realize that up ahead.

08:09.440 --> 08:11.810
Why is there a sun underground?

08:11.810 --> 08:16.740
I'd heard that each floor was 
totally different, but...

08:16.740 --> 08:18.090
Wow.

08:18.550 --> 08:21.670
This is the world you're about to enter.

08:22.140 --> 08:23.530
We're...

08:29.110 --> 08:30.200
Hey, hey.

08:30.200 --> 08:32.320
Let's take a little look around.

08:32.320 --> 08:33.660
That's a bad idea.

08:33.660 --> 08:35.730
The exam's not over until we're back.

08:42.140 --> 08:46.520
It feels like it's been so long 
since I've seen this building.

08:46.970 --> 08:49.760
There were traps on the way home 
too, just like we thought.

08:51.030 --> 08:53.100
Remember what I said? The guild...

08:53.100 --> 08:55.070
...can be mean!

08:55.660 --> 08:57.780
Okay, good work!

08:58.260 --> 09:03.380
With this, the Bronze-class examination 
comes to an end for real.

09:03.730 --> 09:07.480
Does this mean we're Bronze-class now?

09:07.740 --> 09:09.100
Well...

09:09.100 --> 09:11.740
Sister, they'll be fine.

09:12.000 --> 09:13.520
Here's the report.

09:15.850 --> 09:17.030
I see.

09:17.030 --> 09:18.380
In that case...

09:18.380 --> 09:19.810
What's going on?

09:19.810 --> 09:24.320
He was watching us the whole 
time during the exam.

09:25.210 --> 09:27.650
I had no idea!

09:27.650 --> 09:31.490
The exam also tests what 
kind of person you are.

09:31.490 --> 09:36.870
We can't raise your rank if we decide you're 
not the right kind of person for it.

09:36.870 --> 09:39.360
And so we...

09:39.780 --> 09:42.050
You pass without problems.

09:42.910 --> 09:45.890
Now you're real Bronze-class adventurers!

09:46.520 --> 09:48.020
We passed...

09:49.100 --> 09:51.600
Did you hear that, Laura? 
She says we passed!

09:51.960 --> 09:53.570
We did it, Ryze!

09:53.570 --> 09:55.370
I'm so glad we left the village!

09:55.370 --> 09:59.790
Yeah! It was worth coming even when 
Mom and Dad didn't want me to!

09:59.790 --> 10:02.630
What they're saying kind of scares me...

10:01.650 --> 10:03.890
Thanks for coming with me!

10:02.630 --> 10:04.460
Well, it happens a lot.

10:04.460 --> 10:06.470
We need to go tell them.

10:05.060 --> 10:07.990
<i>So I'm Bronze-class again now...</i>

10:11.130 --> 10:14.080
Ryze, Laura. Thanks for 
coming with me today.

10:14.080 --> 10:16.440
No, that's our line.

10:16.440 --> 10:18.620
We won't forget what you taught us today.

10:20.090 --> 10:26.030
Rentt, thanks to you, I think we've 
finally become real adventurers.

10:26.510 --> 10:27.900
Ryze...

10:27.900 --> 10:31.700
I'd like to ask you to keep 
adventuring with us...

10:31.700 --> 10:34.270
but that's impossible, isn't it?

10:35.730 --> 10:41.950
It feels like your goal is 
somehow different than ours.

10:42.390 --> 10:45.490
That's why you told us all that 
stuff during the exam, right?

10:45.490 --> 10:48.800
So we could make it on our own.

10:48.800 --> 10:49.780
Yeah.

10:49.780 --> 10:52.480
You may have only been a part 
of our party for one day,

10:52.480 --> 10:54.750
but you're still a treasured comrade.

10:54.750 --> 10:57.260
Yeah. Let's adventure again sometime!

11:03.410 --> 11:05.280
They're good kids, huh?

11:05.280 --> 11:08.940
Yeah. I felt like a parent 
more than anything.

11:08.940 --> 11:12.070
But they might've been working hard 
to make me feel welcome, too.

11:15.830 --> 11:17.020
Rentt.

11:19.080 --> 11:21.620
I have a question for you.

11:21.620 --> 11:26.050
I apologize for asking when you're 
tired, but will you come with me?

11:26.570 --> 11:31.650
You're sharp enough to know 
what I want to ask, aren't you?

11:32.980 --> 11:36.980
<i>Sheila knows who I really am.</i>

11:38.530 --> 11:42.330
Does the Guild intend to punish 
me for what I've done?

11:42.830 --> 11:45.280
I'm asking the questions here.

11:45.890 --> 11:51.740
If that's the case, I'll never 
come back to this guild.

11:51.740 --> 11:52.840
That's all.

11:53.130 --> 11:53.980
Wait!

11:56.040 --> 11:58.940
I just want to know...

12:00.260 --> 12:04.510
What exactly happened to you?

12:08.000 --> 12:10.360
<i>I thought about running away.</i>

12:10.850 --> 12:13.010
<i>But I couldn't.</i>

12:13.750 --> 12:19.960
<i>Her voice was the voice of a woman who was 
genuinely worried about an old friend.</i>

12:22.960 --> 12:27.590
Sheila, I've got a big problem 
I'm dealing with right now.

12:29.200 --> 12:33.430
I don't want anyone getting 
involved. Not even the guild.

12:34.220 --> 12:39.640
Rentt, I actually haven't told 
the guild about you, yet.

12:42.960 --> 12:45.650
Sheila... Why?

12:46.030 --> 12:49.360
Part of it was that I wasn't sure.

12:49.790 --> 12:53.570
But more than anything, I wanted 
to see the truth for myself.

12:56.240 --> 13:01.960
I've told the man who was watching 
you during the exam a little, but...

13:01.960 --> 13:04.230
He's my brother.

13:04.230 --> 13:06.890
He can keep a secret.

13:08.050 --> 13:12.500
Would you please tell me 
what's happening to you?

13:14.470 --> 13:17.340
It's hard to trust me, isn't it?

13:17.770 --> 13:20.800
So I've prepared this.

13:20.800 --> 13:22.830
A magical contract?

13:23.180 --> 13:24.270
Yes.

13:24.270 --> 13:27.600
If the contract detailed here is broken,

13:27.600 --> 13:30.720
in this case, if I share your secret,

13:30.720 --> 13:34.780
I'll suffer a penalty 
backed by magical force.

13:34.780 --> 13:37.260
If she does not carry out 
her end of the contract,

13:37.260 --> 13:43.930
Sheila Ibarss will leave the guild, travel 
to a country where slavery is legal,

13:43.930 --> 13:47.370
and perform the necessary paperwork to 
transfer ownership of herself to another party.

13:47.850 --> 13:50.850
<i>No, no, no. That's way too heavy!</i>

13:55.680 --> 13:57.730
Why go that far?

14:00.290 --> 14:05.450
I want to help you, and not 
because I'm part of the guild.

14:05.910 --> 14:06.950
Why?

14:07.300 --> 14:13.120
Because it's thanks to you that I grew up.

14:13.650 --> 14:14.910
Sheila...

14:15.320 --> 14:21.340
You don't realize it, but there are a 
lot of people who are grateful to you.

14:23.530 --> 14:25.930
All right. I'll sign.

14:26.350 --> 14:28.100
And then I'll tell you.

14:28.590 --> 14:29.530
Right.

14:32.760 --> 14:36.660
Now, where to begin...

14:36.660 --> 14:38.580
It would be faster to show you, I think.

14:47.740 --> 14:49.330
Terrifying, isn't it?

14:49.870 --> 14:53.570
I bet you regret asking.

14:53.570 --> 14:55.380
No! That's not true...

14:55.750 --> 14:58.220
It's not...

14:58.860 --> 15:05.370
If you're suffering that much...
I'd much rather know.

15:06.380 --> 15:09.160
But how did this happen?

15:09.160 --> 15:11.350
I've turned into a monster.

15:14.820 --> 15:18.050
I'm an undead right now.

15:19.070 --> 15:21.180
Is that possible?

15:23.810 --> 15:28.570
I can see why you'd feel 
distressed hearing this.

15:30.460 --> 15:33.520
So I want you to think about 
it again before you answer...

15:33.520 --> 15:37.840
Can you really help me?

15:40.300 --> 15:44.360
Of course, I have no intention 
of harming anyone.

15:44.360 --> 15:48.510
But that's a different question from 
whether you can believe me or not.

15:49.290 --> 15:50.290
Wait!

15:50.860 --> 15:53.730
I believe you!

15:53.730 --> 15:58.270
I believe you're a monster now, 
and that you won't attack anyone!

15:59.120 --> 16:05.860
Because... Because... you 
were always such a good guy!

16:06.620 --> 16:09.660
Those kids... and me, too...

16:09.660 --> 16:11.410
We all owe you so much.

16:12.570 --> 16:14.940
So I'll help you.

16:17.070 --> 16:21.750
Rentt, if something happens between 
you and the guild, tell me.

16:22.190 --> 16:25.420
I promise... I promise I'll help you.

16:32.910 --> 16:34.170
Oh!

16:34.410 --> 16:36.600
I'm sorry for coming at this hour.

16:36.600 --> 16:41.930
I insisted on coming to speak with you.

16:42.220 --> 16:45.730
Well, you're certainly a rare guest.

16:45.730 --> 16:48.890
Rentt, don't tell me you've 
been messing around with her.

16:48.890 --> 16:50.910
He hasn't.

16:50.910 --> 16:52.900
But I've learned a lot about him.

16:53.310 --> 16:54.620
I see.

16:54.620 --> 16:55.870
Well, that's fine.

16:55.870 --> 16:58.180
Come inside.

16:58.180 --> 17:00.320
It's not very clean, though, I'm afraid.

17:00.760 --> 17:04.770
<i>I cleaned it up before I left...</i>

17:07.250 --> 17:11.290
All right. I suppose I should 
just come out and ask.

17:12.020 --> 17:13.720
How much did you hear?

17:13.720 --> 17:16.940
Rentt told me he's a monster.

17:16.940 --> 17:19.900
And that he's not going to attack anyone.

17:19.900 --> 17:22.740
Oh, that's everything!

17:23.100 --> 17:25.700
And yet you came all the way out here?

17:25.700 --> 17:27.570
That's awfully naïve of you.

17:27.570 --> 17:29.850
What do you mean by that?

17:29.850 --> 17:31.550
Think about it.

17:31.550 --> 17:35.540
Rentt is an undead. 
And I'm a sketchy-looking academic.

17:36.020 --> 17:39.470
What do you think happens to a young 
girl who wanders into the home

17:39.470 --> 17:41.020
of a witch and a monster?

17:43.030 --> 17:50.050
Normally, you could expect to be thrown 
into a boiling pot and end up in my stomach.

17:51.580 --> 17:53.820
Aw, you're no witch.

17:54.300 --> 17:58.750
Everyone knows you're a 
wonderful researcher.

17:58.750 --> 18:02.260
Oh no, that's just what 
I've made everyone think!

18:02.260 --> 18:08.010
Actually, my hobby is going out at night 
to hunt the blood of young maidens!

18:08.010 --> 18:10.270
It makes my skin so beautiful.

18:14.430 --> 18:18.250
That's what Rentt's become.

18:27.510 --> 18:32.930
<i>Lorraine doesn't see Sheila as a person, 
even as she's sitting in front of her.</i>

18:33.740 --> 18:37.430
<i>Depending on her answer, she'll 
eliminate her without hesitation.</i>

18:45.940 --> 18:47.550
I... know that.

18:49.940 --> 18:51.430
I know that.

18:55.190 --> 18:57.800
I see. Good, then.

18:58.850 --> 19:02.530
I'm not saying it to be mean.

19:02.530 --> 19:05.200
And it's late.

19:05.200 --> 19:06.870
Let's have dinner together.

19:07.150 --> 19:08.620
O-Okay!

19:14.300 --> 19:16.170
Thank you for the meal.

19:16.170 --> 19:20.440
I heard you were a good cook, Rentt. I 
guess everyone who said that was right.

19:20.440 --> 19:23.080
I learned in my home village.

19:23.080 --> 19:26.180
It's handy, having him around.

19:26.180 --> 19:28.720
He'll do all the chores for you.

19:29.150 --> 19:33.650
And the price, if I were to 
call it that... is that, for now.

19:38.780 --> 19:40.230
I see.

19:40.590 --> 19:43.820
Ghasts are a type of 
low-ranking vampire, aren't they?

19:43.820 --> 19:45.740
That's right.

19:45.740 --> 19:50.210
Now, you two made a magical contract?

19:50.210 --> 19:54.910
Yes. She won't share who I am.

19:54.910 --> 20:01.080
Yes. But you've been standing out lately...

20:01.610 --> 20:02.690
I have?

20:02.940 --> 20:09.010
There are lots of rookie adventurers going 
missing right now, all over the kingdom.

20:09.010 --> 20:12.680
They haven't just been killed by monsters?

20:12.680 --> 20:15.840
If that happened, their
stuff should be left behind.

20:15.840 --> 20:18.950
The guild is assuming it's 
a series of kidnappings.

20:19.470 --> 20:23.420
I see. And they have a suspect 
who looks extremely suspicious,

20:23.420 --> 20:25.150
and is also highly skilled.

20:25.150 --> 20:28.350
Specifically, Rentt, correct?

20:28.350 --> 20:31.700
He's certainly not acting like a rookie...

20:31.990 --> 20:34.340
Some are spreading rumors 
about him out of jealousy.

20:35.120 --> 20:38.240
Wow, people are jealous of me now?

20:38.240 --> 20:41.460
Hey! It's not a good thing!

20:41.460 --> 20:42.880
That's right.

20:42.880 --> 20:45.600
You're in a delicate position right now.

20:45.600 --> 20:50.640
If it's that bad, I can stop going 
into the labyrinth for a while.

20:50.640 --> 20:54.480
How many days is "a while," exactly?

20:55.010 --> 20:57.260
Three days or so.

20:57.260 --> 20:58.330
What?

21:00.210 --> 21:03.330
Okay... four.

21:09.330 --> 21:11.790
I hope we get someone good.

21:11.790 --> 21:12.700
Yeah.

21:13.150 --> 21:17.210
Once we've got a party, we're going 
down to the second floor again.

21:17.210 --> 21:18.160
Yeah.

21:18.160 --> 21:21.500
We didn't get to go anywhere last time, 
so let's fight a whole lot of monsters!

21:23.490 --> 21:26.130
Work hard, rookies.

21:26.540 --> 21:30.410
Hey, I heard Rentt Vivie 
passed his exam, too.

21:30.410 --> 21:34.230
His skills and personality were just fine.

21:35.060 --> 21:36.490
I see.

21:36.490 --> 21:37.480
Yes.

21:38.310 --> 21:41.150
Speaking of Rentts...

21:41.150 --> 21:44.270
What happened to Rentt Faina?

21:44.830 --> 21:49.000
I was planning on recruiting him 
to the guild once he retired.

21:47.520 --> 21:49.000
"Forgot"?

21:49.000 --> 21:50.700
What am I supposed to do?

21:50.700 --> 21:53.300
Look. One of the new kids is in trouble.

21:53.300 --> 21:54.870
I-I'll go right away!

21:58.450 --> 22:04.700
But Guildmaster, the other Rentt 
is a wonderful adventurer, too!

23:35.680 --> 23:40.010
A New Weapon and Power
